 "findings": {
  "low_level": [
   "The network is opt-W1's template recursion with the min and max exchange (T42) on the fp32 key twiddled to u32: 290 VIMNMX, 142 SHFL, 2 CREDUX.MIN, 16 VOTE, 30 POPC, 8 predicated STS in the N 128 k 16 latency kernel (two network copies), no BSSY, no BRA beyond the harness's five, 0 stack, 0 STL, 0 LDL in every warp cell (T36 check). Registers 30 to 64 in the latency kernel (W1_eager_same 24 to 59), 23 to 32 in the throughput kernel (40 at N 256 k 64), occupancy 8 blocks per SM (6 at N 256 k 64, same as the control). Complete final merge (150 SHFL at N 128 k 16), the k-th word by one SHFL.IDX of position k - 1, then the two-class recovery (two ballots per slot). Registers 35 to 72 in the latency kernel, 23 to 32 (40 at N 256 k 64) in the throughput kernel, occupancy as the control."
  ],
  "algorithmic": [
   "Against the u64 word (W1_eager_same), prefer_smaller_index latency: N 32 570 against 601 (0.95x), N 64 815 against 934 (0.87x), N 128 k 16 1238 against 1918 (0.65x), N 128 k 64 1110 against 2216 (0.50x), N 256 k 16 2105 against 3826 (0.55x), N 256 k 64 1704 against 4650 (0.37x). Throughput 245 to 292 against 165 to 185 Gelem per s (1.33x to 1.77x). Both must-beat cells pass (N 64 k 32 815 at most 840 asked, N 128 k 16 1238 at most 1720).",
   "Against the identical u32 network on bf16 words in the same session (W1x_vimnmx_eager, 512, 695, 1017, 1718 at N 32 to 256) the cost of twiddle, shuffle and recovery is 58, 120, 221 and 387 cycles at IPT 1, 2, 4, 8."
  ],
  "negative": [
   "Dominated by N10_u32_trunc in every cell (66 to 177 cycles, 2 to 10 percent): the complete merge sorts k words that the rank pass never reads. Kept as the measured baseline of the truncation and of the recovery cost."
  ],
  "surprises": [
   "The same cycles at k 4, 16 and 32 for a given N (570, 815, 1238, 2105): the position shuffle and the store predicates do not perturb the schedule here, unlike the fp32 pairs network of T28."
  ],
  "open_questions": [
   "Whether placing the recovered indices into the network positions (sorted output) is worth one shuffle per selected item for the sorted-output pass."
  ]
 },
